      "dom_id": "question-90945",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $2(x+4)^{3}=686.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x+4)^{3}$ term and then taking the $3$rd root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x+4)^{3}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)^{3} & =686 \\\\ (x+4)^{3} & =343\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $3$rd root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{3} & =343 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(x+4)^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{343} \\\\ x+4 & =\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{3}} \\\\ x+4 & =7 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3.$",
